# Cloudflare Pages redirects for HazardNet.
#
# Format: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
# (`from  to  [status]` — the status is optional and defaults to 302.)
#
# This replaced `vercel.json`'s `redirects` array on 2026-10-26, when the
# deployment moved to Cloudflare Pages only (both `hazardnet.live` and
# `www.hazardnet.live` CNAME to `hazardnet.pages.dev`). Cloudflare serves this
# file from the asset root; Vite copies it verbatim into `dist/` because it
# lives in `frontend/public/`.
#
# Deliberately absent #1: `/* /index.html 200`.
#
# The prerenderer emits a real HTML file per route (frontend/scripts/prerender.mjs),
# so known URLs are files and never need a rewrite. An unknown URL falls to
# `404.html`, which Cloudflare Pages serves automatically with a 404 status and
# which is the *noindex* shell — the page still boots the SPA, so a route that is
# real but unlisted (a profile URL, an alert id) renders for the visitor while a
# crawler is told not to index it. A `/* /index.html 200` rule would undo that:
# every unknown URL would answer 200 with the indexable homepage, which is the
# soft-404 case __tests__/seoFoundations.test.js exists to prevent.
#
# Deliberately absent #2: `/api/* /404.html 404` and `/data/* /404.html 404` guards.
# They read as defence-in-depth, but they are the opposite: `/data/*.json` is the site's
# primary read path (ADR 0008) and every route is a real file, so a rule that matches
# those paths can shadow a file that exists. Pages resolves an existing asset first, and
# a path with no asset already lands on 404.html — the guard rules add a way to break
# `/data/` and buy nothing. The invariant they were meant to protect ("no rule may
# swallow /api/* or /data/*") is asserted directly in
# __tests__/securityHeadersParity.test.js instead of encoded as a rule.

/documentation  /docs  301

# Permanent 404 (Phase 4, 2026-10-27) — deliberately NOT a redirect rule.
#
# /api/v1/historical/*, /api/historical and /api/metrics are retired. There is no Function
# for them and no Node host behind this origin, so an unmatched /api/** path already lands
# on the noindex 404 shell. Adding a `/api/* /404.html 404` rule here would shadow real
# assets (see "Deliberately absent #2" above), so this note is the whole guard.
#
#   · historical — the client reads /data/historical/*.json from the CDN (3062 events,
#     1.5 MB). The old handler re-serialised that file: measured parse+stringify
#     median 8.41 ms / p95 11.44 ms against the 10 ms Pages Functions CPU budget.
#   · metrics — a Worker isolate has no Node process series; the one meaningful gauge,
#     hazardnet_forecast_age_hours, is published in /data/freshness.json.
#   · kaggle — still Node-only with a dated R2-artifact plan (Action 21); it is NOT
#     deleted here because frontend/src/hooks/useKaggleAdvisories.ts calls it.
#
# Rollback for the historical deletion is route-restore + removing this comment; visitor
# behaviour is unchanged either way. See docs/ops/owner-actions.md Action 21 and
# docs/ops/pr/phase-4-disposition.md.
